  </p>

  <h2>3. Services</h2>
  <p>
    Ebmeyer Consulting provides consulting, strategy, training and speaking services in the
    fields of artificial intelligence, digitalisation and business development.
  </p>
  <p>
    The services are rendered under the law of mandate (Art. 394 et seq. of the Swiss Code
    of Obligations, CO). What is owed is diligent performance, not a specific commercial
    outcome. No revenue, cost or efficiency targets are warranted.
  </p>
  <p>
    Ebmeyer Consulting may engage partners and specialists to perform the services and
    remains the Client's point of contact in such cases. Services that the Client agrees and
    settles directly with third parties (such as technical implementation, design, licences
    or hosting) are not part of this contract.
  </p>
  <p>
    Ebmeyer Consulting does not provide legal, tax, financial or medical advice. All
    entrepreneurial decisions are taken by the Client on its own responsibility.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Client's Duty to Cooperate</h2>
  <p>
    The Client shall provide, in good time and in full, all information, documents and
    access required for the performance of the services, and shall designate a contact
    person authorised to take decisions. Queries and agreed preparatory tasks shall be dealt
    with within the agreed deadline.
  </p>
  <p>
    For on-site appointments, the Client shall provide suitable premises, a stable internet
    connection, the necessary presentation equipment and – in the case of training sessions
    – working devices for the participants.
  </p>
  <p>
    Delays attributable to the Client extend the agreed dates accordingly. Where this
    results in work beyond the agreed scope of services, such work will be quoted separately
    and performed only after written approval.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Appointments, Rescheduling and Cancellation</h2>
  <p>
    Appointments become binding upon written confirmation. If the Client reschedules or
    cancels a confirmed appointment, the following applies:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>up to 14 calendar days in advance: free of charge, once per appointment</li>
    <li>13 to 7 calendar days in advance: 50 per cent of the fee attributable to the appointment</li>
    <li>less than 7 calendar days in advance or non-attendance: 100 per cent</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Travel and incidental costs already incurred and no longer cancellable are payable in
    addition.
  </p>
  <p>
    If Ebmeyer Consulting is prevented from attending, an alternative date will be offered.
    Where this is not possible, payments already made for the cancelled appointment will be
    refunded.
  </p>
  <p>
    Sessions not taken within a multi-part programme expire 12 months after the start of the
    programme.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Fees and Payment</h2>
  <p>
    All prices are quoted in Swiss francs and exclusive of value added tax. Ebmeyer
    Consulting is currently not liable for VAT; should VAT liability arise, value added tax
    will be charged in addition.
  </p>
  <p>
    Remuneration is project-based, as a fixed fee for the scope of services defined in the
    quotation. The fee is determined by the scope, complexity and value of the services, not
    by the actual time spent. There is no entitlement to a reduction of the fee if less time
    is required.
  </p>
  <p>
    Not included in the fee and payable in addition are travel and accommodation costs,
    licence and tool costs, services of engaged third parties, and printing, material and
    room costs. For on-site appointments, a travel flat rate as stated in the quotation will
    be charged.
  </p>
  <p>
    Unless agreed otherwise, 50 per cent of the fee is due upon order confirmation and 50
    per cent upon completion. For multi-phase programmes, the fee falls due phase by phase,
    in each case at the start of the relevant phase. Workshops, seminars and speaking
    engagements are payable in full before the event date.
  </p>
  <p>
    Invoices are payable within 14 calendar days without deduction. After expiry of the
    payment period, default interest of 5 per cent per annum is owed (Art. 104 CO). In the
    event of payment default, Ebmeyer Consulting may suspend performance of the services.
  </p>
  <p>
    Discounts or special conditions apply only to the specific individual order designated
    and create no entitlement in respect of subsequent orders.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Revision Rounds and Acceptance</h2>
  <p>
    The fee includes one revision round per deliverable unless the quotation provides
    otherwise. Feedback shall be given in consolidated form and in writing within 10 working
    days of delivery.
  </p>
  <p>
    Further revision rounds as well as changes or extensions to the agreed scope of services
    are not included in the fee. They will be quoted separately and carried out only after
    written approval.
  </p>
  <p>
    If no written objection is raised within 10 working days, or if the Client uses the
    deliverable productively, the deliverable is deemed accepted.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Rights of Use</h2>
  <p>
    All rights to the methods, models, templates, rule sets, prompt and system
    architectures, training materials and presentations contributed or developed by Ebmeyer
    Consulting remain with Ebmeyer Consulting.
  </p>
  <p>
    Upon full payment, the Client receives a non-exclusive, non-transferable right of
    unlimited duration to use the deliverables created for it within its own organisation or
    for its own purposes.
  </p>
  <p>
    Without written consent, the following are not permitted in particular: transfer or sale
    to third parties, use for the Client's own paid consulting or training offerings, and
    use for training artificial intelligence models.
  </p>
  <p>
    Recordings of workshops, training sessions and presentations require prior written
    consent. Course materials are intended exclusively for the personal use of participants.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Client warrants that it holds the necessary rights to all materials it provides.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Use of Artificial Intelligence</h2>
  <p>
    Ebmeyer Consulting uses artificial intelligence systems as well as tools and services
    provided by third parties to deliver its services.
  </p>
  <p>
    Results produced by AI-supported systems are generated on a probabilistic basis and may
    be incomplete, outdated or factually incorrect. They must be reviewed by the Client
    before use. Ebmeyer Consulting gives no warranty as to the accuracy, completeness or
    reproducibility of AI-generated content.
  </p>
  <p>
    The availability, functionality, pricing and terms of use of third-party tools are
    beyond the control of Ebmeyer Consulting. The Client obtains any required licences and
    subscriptions in its own name and at its own expense.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Client shall ensure that no sensitive personal data, professional or official
    secrets, health data and no data relating to children or young people are entered into
    AI systems, unless expressly agreed in writing. Without such an agreement, the
    processing of such data is expressly excluded from the scope of services.
  </p>
  <p>
    Following handover of an AI assistant, operation, maintenance, monitoring and updating
    are the responsibility of the Client. Support and further development are owed only
    under a separate agreement.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Confidentiality and Data Protection</h2>
  <p>
    Both parties shall treat non-public information of the other party as confidential and
    use it solely for the performance of the contract. This obligation applies for the term
    of the contract and for three years thereafter.
  </p>
  <p>
    Ebmeyer Consulting processes personal data in accordance with the Swiss Federal Act on
    Data Protection (FADP) and, where applicable, the GDPR. Details are set out in the
    <a href="/en/privacy/">privacy policy</a> at www.ebmeyer-consulting.ch.
  </p>
  <p>
    Ebmeyer Consulting does not process personal data on behalf of the Client. The service
    model is designed so that the Client sets up and operates its AI applications
    independently and on its own responsibility; control over the data remains with the
    Client. For its own service delivery, Ebmeyer Consulting may use providers such as
    cloud, AI and collaboration services.
  </p>

  <h2>11. References</h2>
  <p>
    Ebmeyer Consulting may name the Client's name and logo as well as a general,
