  </p>
  <p>
    Either party may terminate the contract with immediate effect for good cause, in
    particular in the event of a serious breach of contract or payment default exceeding 30
    days despite a reminder.
  </p>

  <h2>15. Force Majeure</h2>
  <p>
    Events beyond a party's control – such as natural events, official orders, strikes,
    cyberattacks or the failure of telecommunications, cloud or AI services – release the
    affected party from its performance obligations for the duration of the impediment. If
    the event lasts longer than 60 calendar days, either party may withdraw from the
    contract; services already rendered shall be remunerated.
  </p>

